			"Message": "feat(Air): Implement DNS-based security with local DNS resolver\n\nThis commit introduces a defense-in-depth security measure by routing all HTTP traffic through a local DNS server, ensuring `*.editor.land` domains resolve exclusively to `127.x.x.x` loopback addresses.\n\n**New HTTP Module (`Source/HTTP/`)**\n- Created `Source/HTTP/client.rs` with `secured_client()`, `secured_client_builder()`, and `secured_client_with_timeout()` functions\n- These functions configure reqwest HTTP clients to use a custom DNS resolver that overrides system DNS\n- The resolver leverages the Mist workspace dependency (Hickory DNS server) to enforce localhost-only resolution for `*.editor.land` domains\n- Added comprehensive documentation explaining the security model and usage examples\n\n**Security Integration Points**\n- Updated `Source/Downloader/mod.rs` to use the secured HTTP client with DNS override\n- Updated `Source/Updates/mod.rs` to use secured clients for update checks and downloads\n- Updated `Source/Vine/Server/AirVinegRPCService.rs` to use secured clients for gRPC download streaming\n\n**Dependency Updates**\n- Added `anyhow` and `Mist` (workspace dependencies)\n- Updated `rustls-native-certs` from 0.7 to 0.8 (with API changes for the new CertificateResult struct)\n- Updated `windows` crate from 0.58 to 0.62\n- Added `tokio-test` and `futures` as dev-dependencies\n\n**Code Quality**\n- Added `#[allow(dead_code)]` attributes to suppress warnings for unused structs/functions in logging, metrics, updates, and plugins modules\n- Fixed minor formatting and doc comment issues\n- Added new integration test file `tests/dns_resolver_tests.rs` with comprehensive tests for DNS resolution, security validation, caching, and concurrent queries\n\n**Impact**: This change ensures that all network communication with Land's editor services is protected against DNS spoofing and cache poisoning attacks by enforcing that all `*.editor.land` domains resolve only to localhost addresses.",
