			"Message": "refactor(Air): Improve documentation and cleanup dead code\n\nThis commit enhances documentation quality and removes unused code across the\nAir background daemon, while also fixing a potential issue in the gRPC download\nstreaming service.\n\n**Documentation Improvements**\n\n- Added \"Deep Dive & Component Breakdown\" section to README with source file\n  references\n- Changed ASCII diagram code blocks to `text` format to prevent Rustdoc warnings\n- Applied consistent backtick escaping for type names, URLs, and example values\n  in doc comments\n- Standardized TODO formatting from `[BRACKETS]` to `` `BACKTICKS` `` style\n\n**Dead Code Cleanup**\n\n- Removed unused imports: `IndexingConfig`, `CreateNewIndex`, `CertificateDer`,\n  `ServerName`, `RngCore`\n- Prefixed unused variables and parameters with underscore to satisfy compiler\n  warnings\n- Fixed unused assignment pattern in `ValidateAndRepairIndex`\n\n**gRPC Download Fix**\n\n- Changed `total_size` from `u64` to `Option<u64>` in\n  `AirVinegRPCService::Download` to properly handle responses without\n  `Content-Length` header\n- Updated progress calculation to safely unwrap the optional size\n\n**Submodule Update**\n\n- Updated `Documentation/Rust` submodule to latest commit",
